# Copy to .env and fill in. The .env file is not committed.

# The language-understanding layer (OpenRouter). Without this key the app still
# runs — questions are parsed by the fallback rule parser, and every figure is
# still computed by the scoring engine from the data. All that is lost is the
# ability to understand free-form sentences well.
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=

# Optional, and best LEFT EMPTY. Empty = use the free model chain in
# src/lib/server/llm.ts, tried in order until one answers — which matters because
# free models are often busy (429/503) or slow. Set = pin to that one model, with
# no fallbacks. Read at runtime, so changing it on Vercel is just an Environment
# Variable edit — no rebuild needed. Whichever is active can be checked at
# GET /api/meta.
OPENROUTER_MODEL=

# The MAPID MAPS Map Service key — the 24-character one the MAPID Dashboard hands
# out under MAP SERVICES. This is the setting to use. The app builds the style URL
# from it, following MAPID's documented shape
# (https://v2.basemap.mapid.io/styles/<style>/style.json?key=<key>), and picks the
# light or dark style to match the theme the reader is on. Empty and an open raster
# basemap (OpenStreetMap/CARTO) is used instead.
PUBLIC_MAPID_MAP_KEY=

# Optional, and only for a style this app does not know about: a self-hosted one, a
# proxy, or one MAPID publishes after this was written. A FULL URL. Set, it wins over
# PUBLIC_MAPID_MAP_KEY and the theme no longer follows the reader.
# A bare KEY left in here still works: this is where the key used to go, so the app
# reads it as one rather than telling you it is in the wrong box.
PUBLIC_MAPID_STYLE_URL=

# The MAPID API key (read-only) — used by the data scripts, not by the app.
# Without it `scripts/fetch-mapid.mjs` will not run (`search-mapid.mjs` does not
# need it — the premium catalogue endpoint is open without authentication); the
# app still runs, because it reads the JSON files those scripts produced.
# It may also be supplied as an environment variable, and the environment wins over
# the contents of this file. Get one from the MAPID Dashboard → API Keys.
# Note: this key is different from the Map Service key in PUBLIC_MAPID_MAP_KEY.
MAPID_API_KEY=

# Optional. Your own GEO MAPID project. It plays two roles at once: the project
# whose layers get scanned, AND the "read ticket" into the premium data catalogue —
# get_layer checks ownership of the project_id sent, not the layer's membership of
# it, so catalogue datasets can be read without being imported. It therefore has to
# be a project genuinely owned by the account holding MAPID_API_KEY. Empty = use the
# default project (6a7c1672fb8d434002151fa7).
#
# Do NOT point this at a project someone shared with you. get_layer_list answers
# 403 "Not owner" for a project you do not own, and the premium reads would go down
# with it, because the ticket has to be yours. See docs/04-data-mapid.md §4.
MAPID_PROJECT_ID=

# The competition's field surveys (Struk Go, Menu Go, Properti Go) and the community
# notes filed beside them need NO key and no layer id. They are not published as
# layers at all: MAPID Apps serves them from its own public endpoints, which is what
# `node scripts/fetch-missions.mjs` reads. Nothing to set here.

# MongoDB. THIS IS THE SWITCH between the two ways SpotOn runs.
#
# Set, and accounts, sessions and quotas are stored in that cluster: signing in wants an
# address and a password, and what somebody buys is still there next week.
#
# EMPTY = DEMO MODE, and that is a supported way to run this, not a broken one. There is
# one account, signing in is a single button with no password, and the records live in
# the server's memory until it restarts. Everything else is identical — the same three
# tiers, the same weekly allowances, the same two meters counting down — because only the
# storage changes. It is the same rule the rest of the file follows: the map still draws
# without a MAPID key and questions are still answered without a model key, so the app
# has to be openable from a bare clone with nothing filled in.
#
# The interface says which mode it is in rather than leaving it to be discovered: the
# sign-in page explains it, and the account page repeats it beside the account itself.
#
# Shape: mongodb+srv://<user>:<password>@<cluster>/?retryWrites=true&w=majority
MONGODB_URI=

# Optional. The database inside that cluster. Empty = `spoton`. The URI may name one of
# its own after the host, and this wins over that.
MONGODB_DB=
